‪John.

225
00:10:07,565 --> 00:10:08,482
‪Yes?

226
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:11,277
‪-Am I finally heading upstairs?
‪-What?

227
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:14,405
‪Do I finally get to enjoy a warm meal too?

228
00:10:15,531 --> 00:10:17,033
‪Your play earlier was really impressive.

229
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:18,242
‪Thank you.

230
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:21,954
‪You should've taken me up on my offer.

231
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:24,415
‪Huh?

232
00:10:24,957 --> 00:10:29,378
‪You all went through a lot yesterday.

233
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:31,922
‪But someone made a particularly sharp call

234
00:10:32,006 --> 00:10:35,051
‪and should be rewarded for surviving
‪and making it through another day.

235
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:37,303
‪I'll be giving this to XITSUH.

236
00:10:37,970 --> 00:10:39,305
‪Thank you, Dong-min.

237
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:42,933
‪Thank you.

238
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,436
‪Yurisa, you understand, right?

239
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:46,479
‪-Congrats.
‪-Of course.

240
00:10:46,562 --> 00:10:50,107
<i>‪XITSUH will be going to the living area.</i>

241
00:10:51,275 --> 00:10:56,072
<i>‪The players for both the living area</i>
<i>‪and the prison have been decided.</i>

242
00:11:00,368 --> 00:11:03,412
‪I believe now seems like
‪the most fitting time.

243
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:09,168
‪I'd like to use the salvation token.

244
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,176
‪-What? So that's it?
‪-What is that?

245
00:11:17,259 --> 00:11:18,636
<i>‪Jung Won-young,</i>

246
00:11:18,719 --> 00:11:20,805
<i>‪you have used the salvation token.</i>

247
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:23,057
<i>‪I choose Shindong.</i>

248
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:26,519
<i>‪Shindong is eliminated</i>
<i>‪from </i>‪The Devil's Plan.

249
00:11:26,602 --> 00:11:29,688
<i>‪Jung Won-young,</i>
<i>‪you will be going to the living area</i>

250
00:11:29,772 --> 00:11:31,440
<i>‪instead of prison.</i>

251
00:11:32,316 --> 00:11:33,317
<i>‪As a result,</i>

252
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:35,694
<i>‪the lowest-ranked player</i>
<i>‪of the living area,</i>

253
00:11:35,778 --> 00:11:37,071
<i>‪XITSUH,</i>

254
00:11:37,571 --> 00:11:39,240
<i>‪-will be going to prison.</i>
‪-Come on.

255
00:11:39,907 --> 00:11:41,117
‪Are you kidding me?

256
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:04,390
‪THE DEVIL'S PLAN: DEAD AGAIN

257
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:05,766
<i>‪XITSUH</i>

258
00:12:06,267 --> 00:12:07,935
<i>‪-will be going to prison.</i>
‪-Come on.

259
00:12:08,602 --> 00:12:09,645
‪Are you kidding me?

260
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,108
‪Sorry.

261
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:16,944
‪You poor thing.

262
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:19,280
‪-Looks like you're coming with me.
‪-Oh no.

263
00:12:19,363 --> 00:12:22,032
<i>‪-The Devil's Plan</i>‪ is so fun!
‪-Guess you're stuck with me.

264
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:23,159
‪What on earth?

265
00:12:23,242 --> 00:12:25,411
‪-You're not going anywhere, XITSUH.
‪-So fun!

266
00:12:25,494 --> 00:12:26,537
‪-Let's play.
‪-Another game!

267
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:31,083
<i>‪The players for both the living area</i>
<i>‪and the prison have been decided.</i>

268
00:12:32,209 --> 00:12:34,086
‪-I still appreciate it.
<i>‪-Jang Dong-min,</i>

269
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:36,589
<i>‪Hyun Kyung-lyul,</i>

270
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:39,091
<i>‪and Jung Won-young</i>
<i>‪will be going to the living area.</i>

271
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:40,801
<i>‪XITSUH,</i>

272
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:42,261
<i>‪John Park,</i>

273
00:12:42,344 --> 00:12:45,306
<i>‪and Yurisa will be going to prison.</i>

274
00:12:45,389 --> 00:12:46,390
‪-Thank you.
‪-Hey, XITSUH.

275
00:12:46,474 --> 00:12:47,475
‪-Sorry.
‪-Don't be.

276
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:48,893
‪-See you tomorrow.
‪-At the main match.

277
00:12:48,976 --> 00:12:49,810
‪You need your coffee tomorrow.

278
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:51,604
‪-Don't worry, I'll make it.
‪-My most reliable…

279
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:52,688
‪-Okay.
‪-I won't go home.

280
00:12:52,771 --> 00:12:54,398
‪-Once I make it up there,
‪-You will.

281
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:57,318
‪-the prison trio will be there.
‪-It'll be three-on-one.

282
00:12:57,401 --> 00:12:59,570
‪-Sorry, Yurisa.
‪-It's fine.

283
00:12:59,653 --> 00:13:00,821
‪-Listen.
‪-Can't avoid it.

284
00:13:00,905 --> 00:13:03,032
‪You just need to survive and make it back.

285
00:13:03,115 --> 00:13:04,742
‪Got it?

286
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:09,872
<i>‪Now, please make your way</i>
<i>‪to your respective living spaces.</i>

287
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:12,708
<i>‪The Devil's </i><i>‪Plan</i>‪ is so fun!

288
00:13:12,791 --> 00:13:15,169
‪-Come with me, XITSUH.
‪-No hope for escape.

289
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:18,130
‪-See you later.
‪-See you in the morning.

290
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:20,299
‪Damn this game.

291
00:13:20,382 --> 00:13:21,383
‪Sorry.

292
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:22,676
‪Enjoy your stay.

293
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,053
‪That was so funny.

294
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:27,264
‪That was perfect timing.

295
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:44,657
‪You must be kidding me.

296
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:48,911
<i>‪I couldn't just say no to a second chance.</i>

297
00:13:48,994 --> 00:13:50,913
<i>‪I came here to win, after all.</i>

298
00:13:50,996 --> 00:13:54,416
<i>‪I decided to open the red door</i>
<i>‪for another chance to win.</i>

299
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:58,712
‪Yeah, you're right.

300
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:01,632
‪-Oh jeez.
‪-Dong-jae!

301
00:14:02,466 --> 00:14:03,676
‪-What's this?
‪-Why are you here?

302
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:06,428
‪Where are we?
‪Why are there only three of us?

303
00:14:06,512 --> 00:14:07,763
‪This is the exile zone.

304
00:14:07,846 --> 00:14:10,766
<i>‪-Welcome to the exile zone.</i>
<i>‪-</i>‪Was this always here?

305
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:12,810
‪Wait, he said he'd be in trouble
‪if you came.

306
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:13,811
‪Teary trouble.

307
00:14:13,894 --> 00:14:15,312
‪What's wrong? Come on now.

308
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:16,522
‪Teary trouble.

309
00:14:16,605 --> 00:14:19,149
‪Why are you crying? Stop it.

310
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:21,360
‪I guess he really meant it.

311
00:14:26,448 --> 00:14:28,701
<i>‪Hyun-min started crying when he saw me.</i>

312
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:31,328
<i>‪And when he did,</i>

313
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:34,373
<i>‪all the emotions from yesterday</i>
<i>‪came rushing in.</i>

314
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:37,001
<i>‪So I got a little choked up.</i>

315
00:14:37,585 --> 00:14:40,337
‪Seriously, why are you here?

316
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:41,505
‪Good job hanging in there.

317
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:51,932
‪I didn't know how to take that.

318
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:55,603
‪I guess it was trouble,
‪but I didn't know why.

319
00:14:55,686 --> 00:14:57,313
<i>‪I mean, I have no idea what's going on.</i>

320
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:01,525
‪It was so awkward for me.
‪I'm struggling over here, you know.

321
00:15:02,151 --> 00:15:03,444
‪Unbelievable.

322
00:15:03,986 --> 00:15:05,738
‪This might not sound right, but welcome.

323
00:15:05,821 --> 00:15:07,823
‪-You've been through so much.
‪-What is this place?

324
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,325
‪This is the exile zone.

325
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:10,409
‪And what do we do here?

326
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:11,952
‪-Sit down first.
‪-We'll fill you in.

327
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:14,038
‪-Please explain, senior colleagues.
‪-We will.

328
00:15:14,121 --> 00:15:15,956
‪Before we do, tell us this.

329
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,583
‪-But--
‪-Who competed at the last prison match?

330
00:15:17,666 --> 00:15:19,460
‪-Yeah, give us the rundown.
‪-Yesterday.

331
00:15:19,543 --> 00:15:20,461
‪Yesterday,

332
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:22,880
‪-during the game,
‪-Yeah?

333
00:15:22,963 --> 00:15:24,632
‪-Hyun-gyu
‪-Okay.

334
00:15:24,715 --> 00:15:26,008
‪had a panic attack.

335
00:15:26,091 --> 00:15:27,551
‪-For real?
‪-Yeah.

336
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:31,180
‪So he voluntarily withdrew
‪from the competition yesterday.

337
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:33,057
‪-Seriously?
‪-No way.

338
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,935
‪-Hyun-gyu did?
‪-It happened all of a sudden.

339
00:15:36,018 --> 00:15:37,645
‪-The stress must've been overwhelming.
‪-Right.

340
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:39,188
‪-So…
‪-Yeah, it's tough.

341
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:41,649
‪-So that's why no one came here yesterday.
‪-Yeah.

342
00:15:42,149 --> 00:15:43,108
‪You did well.

343
00:15:43,609 --> 00:15:45,945
‪-Okay, let us explain now.
‪-This is the exile zone.

344
00:15:46,028 --> 00:15:47,613
‪-This place--
‪-We can tell Dong-jae.

345
00:15:48,197 --> 00:15:49,114
‪-Are you sure?
‪-Yes.

346
00:15:49,782 --> 00:15:51,867
‪Okay, we'll tell you everything we know.

347
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:54,119
‪-So this is how you survive here.
‪-Okay.

348
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:56,246
‪-There are two ways.
‪-Okay.

349
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:57,957
‪-There's a route to the hidden stage.
‪-Okay.

350
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,166
‪-Today's done.
‪-A hidden mission.

351
00:15:59,249 --> 00:16:01,627
‪The order's a bit backed up,
‪so you won't be able to take it on.

352
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:02,878
‪-Got it.
‪-It doesn't apply to you.

353
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:04,880
‪-I have no complaints whatsoever.
‪-Okay.

354
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:07,174
‪-Don't worry about that.
‪-So Seok-jin went today.

355
00:16:07,257 --> 00:16:09,677
‪That was our first attempt, and he failed.

356
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:11,679
‪-And I'm up tomorrow.
‪-I see.

357
00:16:11,762 --> 00:16:13,055
‪-It's one chance per day.
‪-Right.

358
00:16:14,056 --> 00:16:15,683
‪I don't know what it is, but good luck.

359
00:16:15,766 --> 00:16:17,267
‪-I only get a chance if she fails.
‪-Oh, yeah?

360
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:19,144
‪-He's next if I fail.
‪-Is he?

361
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:20,604
‪You can't go if someone succeeds?

362
00:16:20,688 --> 00:16:22,022
‪-No.
‪-Only one person can succeed.

363
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:23,273
‪-That's one of two ways.
‪-That's it?

364
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:24,650
‪-There's a second way.
‪-Okay.

365
00:16:24,733 --> 00:16:27,361
‪-Do you see how there are four corners?
‪-Yeah.

366
00:16:27,444 --> 00:16:28,487
‪There are platforms,

367
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:31,448
‪and they sink and come up again
‪like it's a game show.

368
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:32,908
‪Then the exile zone match happens.

369
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,243
‪-With whom?
‪-All of us.

370
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:38,205
‪They hold the exile zone matches to keep
‪the numbers to four players or less.

371
00:16:38,288 --> 00:16:42,418
‪On the last day, one person here
‪gets picked as the winner.

372
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:44,128
‪-Then they get to return.
‪-That person returns.

373
00:16:44,628 --> 00:16:47,840
‪So at most,
‪two players can get back into the game.

374
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:49,550
‪-So--
‪-I thought I was being eliminated,

375
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:51,010
‪so I didn't eat anything before I left.

376
00:16:51,093 --> 00:16:53,220
‪-I was upset and wanted to go home.
‪-They give us sandwiches.

377
00:16:53,303 --> 00:16:55,014
‪-There should be fresh ones now.
‪-You're right.

378
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:56,515
‪-I guess not.
‪-Not yet?

379
00:16:56,598 --> 00:16:57,725
‪-Plain bread is fine.
‪-But…

380
00:16:57,808 --> 00:16:59,184
‪-May I?
‪-This is plain bread. Go on.

381
00:16:59,268 --> 00:17:01,770
‪-Have this too.
‪-The next batch will have some filling.

382
00:17:02,354 --> 00:17:03,939
‪It's better than prison food.

383
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,150
‪-Anyway, Dong-jae.
‪-It's good to see you.

384
00:17:06,233 --> 00:17:08,527
‪I know it's a lot to take in.

385
00:17:08,610 --> 00:17:10,487
‪-But this is a peaceful place.
‪-Likewise.

386
00:17:10,571 --> 00:17:12,823
‪The bathroom is to the left downstairs.

387
00:17:12,906 --> 00:17:14,324
‪-Okay.
‪-Your white outfit will be there.

388
00:17:14,408 --> 00:17:15,743
‪-Go and get changed.
‪-Yeah, do that.

389
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:17,327
‪-So I need to change.
‪-Yeah.

390
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:20,622
‪-Don't be cheeky, okay?
‪-Don't sport the living area's uniform.

391
00:17:21,123 --> 00:17:22,332
‪I'll be back.

392
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:29,673
‪I can't believe I cried again today.

393
00:17:33,552 --> 00:17:34,636
‪What's wrong with me?

394
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:37,806
‪I seriously didn't expect you
‪to just start crying like that.

395
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:39,516
‪Did you see me scratching my head?

396
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:45,272
‪I didn't know what to do with myself.

397
00:17:46,732 --> 00:17:49,068
‪Hold on, it's already past six.

398
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:53,572
‪Time goes faster with a new member.

399
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:55,157
‪Yeah, it's nice.

400
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,408
‪It's a nice dopamine rush.

401
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:58,911
‪I should practice.

402
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:01,371
‪The magic square or whatever.

403
00:18:02,247 --> 00:18:03,457
‪What even is this?

404
00:18:10,964 --> 00:18:14,176
<i>‪Hyun-min actually dropped a hint earlier.</i>

405
00:18:14,259 --> 00:18:15,385
‪Remainders.

406
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:17,221
‪When he first explained the magic square,

407
00:18:17,304 --> 00:18:21,016
‪I specifically remember him saying
‪you need to use the remainders.

408
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:24,603
‪A number with each possible remainder
‪when divided by seven must go in each set.

409
00:18:24,686 --> 00:18:26,772
‪It could be 7 times 1 plus 0,

410
00:18:26,855 --> 00:18:28,732
‪or it could be 7 times 2 plus 1, right?

411
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:30,984
<i>‪So I tried it out,</i>

412
00:18:31,068 --> 00:18:33,195
<i>‪wondering if I could reach 49 that way.</i>

413
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:39,409
<i>‪I went diagonally this way,</i>
<i>‪1, 8, 15, and so on.</i>

414
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:43,664
<i>‪Since the different remainders</i>
<i>‪all line up on top of each other,</i>

415
00:18:43,747 --> 00:18:45,582
<i>‪I assumed the sums should match too.</i>

416
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:50,379
<i>‪But the top line didn't make sense.</i>
<i>‪The numbers were too low.</i>

417
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:51,421
<i>‪So I thought that wasn't it.</i>

418
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:53,590
‪Did you figure out the secret?

419
00:18:53,674 --> 00:18:55,342
‪I'm working on it.

420
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:58,262
‪Are you working on
‪a magic square right now?

421
00:18:58,345 --> 00:19:00,597
‪-She's trying to put one together.
‪-With my almonds.

422
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:01,557
‪That's wild.

423
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:04,184
‪-With almonds…
‪-Didn't you say you could do a 7-by-7?

424
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:06,770
‪I told you I hadn't tried the one
‪where the numbers go up to 49 yet.

425
00:19:06,854 --> 00:19:08,981
‪-The version where the number goes to 49?
‪-Yeah.

426
00:19:09,064 --> 00:19:10,607
‪But would they really do that to us?

427
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:13,235
‪-Let's be real.
‪-Yeah?

428
00:19:13,318 --> 00:19:14,945
‪That'd be impossible
‪without a pen and paper.

429
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:17,614
‪Why else would Seok-jin have failed?

430
00:19:17,698 --> 00:19:19,324
‪It must've been really hard.

431
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:22,369
‪-So you think it's a difficult level?
‪-I think I cracked a 4-by-4 as a kid.

432
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:23,662
‪That's doable.

433
00:19:23,745 --> 00:19:25,080
‪Really? So that's fine?

434
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:26,456
‪Does it get rough from a 5-by-5?

435
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:28,876
‪If you know the algorithm,
‪you can do them all.

436
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:30,878
‪But if you don't,

437
00:19:30,961 --> 00:19:32,045
‪it's impossible.

438
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:37,301
‪-Realistically, you just can't.
‪-That's very discouraging.

439
00:19:37,384 --> 00:19:40,095
‪As Hyun-min said,
‪if it's filling in 1 through 49,

440
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:42,014
‪I'd be completely lost.

441
00:19:42,097 --> 00:19:44,474
<i>‪So I'm definitely feeling nervous.</i>

442
00:19:44,558 --> 00:19:46,685
‪Honestly, 1 through 49…

443
00:19:47,644 --> 00:19:49,271
‪-You can't do it.
‪-I can't wrap my head around it.

444
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:51,607
‪-Realistically speaking, you can't do it.
‪-I can't do it.

445
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:52,858
‪Right.

446
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:54,735
‪Isn't the secret
‪planting 25 in the center?

447
00:19:56,695 --> 00:19:58,655
‪That's the character for number one.

448
00:19:58,739 --> 00:19:59,990
‪-This?
‪-Yeah.

449
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:03,785
‪-That's one.
‪-That means "one" in this place.

450
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:05,787
‪That's how they write it here.

451
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:08,415
‪-How did you even figure that out?
‪-So…

452
00:20:08,498 --> 00:20:11,919
‪-You all are insane.
‪-It's all connected.

453
00:20:12,002 --> 00:20:14,213
‪Man, you all are something else.

454
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:18,217
‪-What?
‪-Hold on. Today too?

455
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:20,636
‪I guess there's an exile zone match.

456
00:20:24,181 --> 00:20:26,141
‪Shall we make a toast?

457
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:27,893
‪-Come on.
‪-That was nice while it lasted.

458
00:20:27,976 --> 00:20:29,436
‪We don't have time to say goodbye later.

459
00:20:29,519 --> 00:20:31,188
‪-Let's do this.
‪-They take the loser away immediately.

460
00:20:31,271 --> 00:20:32,981
‪-Good luck.
‪-Good luck.

461
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:36,568
<i>‪We will now begin the exile zone match.</i>

462
00:20:37,152 --> 00:20:39,071
<i>‪Please make your way</i>

463
00:20:39,154 --> 00:20:40,614
‪-Let's go!
‪<i>-to a spot of your choice.</i>

464
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:44,576
‪Let's do this. Go!

465
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:45,619
‪-Good luck!
‪-Let's go!

466
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:48,622
<i>‪The fifth exile zone match is</i>

467
00:20:49,206 --> 00:20:50,666
<i>‪Symmetrical Puzzle.</i>

468
00:20:52,042 --> 00:20:53,126
<i>‪In Symmetrical Puzzle,</i>

469
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:55,504
<i>‪players have to combine</i>
<i>‪the given puzzle pieces</i>

470
00:20:55,587 --> 00:20:58,382
<i>‪to form a single shape.</i>

471
00:20:59,091 --> 00:21:01,301
<i>‪The completed puzzle</i>
<i>‪must form a symmetrical shape,</i>

472
00:21:01,385 --> 00:21:03,553
<i>‪where the left and right sides</i>

473
00:21:03,637 --> 00:21:07,432
<i>‪mirror each other exactly</i>
<i>‪around a single axis.</i>

474
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:12,729
<i>‪However, the puzzle pieces</i>
<i>‪cannot be flipped over.</i>

475
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:18,318
<i>‪Players must press the buzzer</i>
<i>‪once the three puzzles of different colors</i>

476
00:21:18,402 --> 00:21:20,028
<i>‪have been completed.</i>

477
00:21:20,654 --> 00:21:23,699
<i>‪The one player who fails</i>
<i>‪to complete the puzzle by the end</i>

478
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:26,118
<i>‪will go home.</i>

479
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:31,164
<i>‪We will now give you</i>
<i>‪the lock combination for the box.</i>

480
00:21:31,748 --> 00:21:35,627
<i>‪Nine, nine, one.</i>

481
00:21:35,711 --> 00:21:37,754
<i>‪The game has begun.</i>

482
00:21:43,051 --> 00:21:44,761
<i>‪The rules were pretty simple,</i>

483
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:47,556
<i>‪and there weren't that many pieces,</i>

484
00:21:47,639 --> 00:21:50,183
<i>‪so I thought it'd be a race against time.</i>

485
00:21:50,267 --> 00:21:52,269
<i>‪It left me a bit rattled in the beginning.</i>

486
00:21:53,895 --> 00:21:59,192
<i>‪I personally haven't really done</i>
<i>‪puzzles like this since I was a kid.</i>

487
00:21:59,276 --> 00:22:02,779
‪If I'm being honest,
‪I was really caught off guard at first.

488
00:22:04,072 --> 00:22:07,159
<i>‪I thought, "Shapes? I should be fine."</i>

489
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:24,885
<i>‪The blue one was pretty easy.</i>

490
00:22:24,968 --> 00:22:27,471
<i>‪I noticed there were matching angles,</i>

491
00:22:27,554 --> 00:22:29,890
<i>‪so to make them mirror each other,</i>

492
00:22:29,973 --> 00:22:32,768
<i>‪I just lined them up at the center.</i>

493
00:22:32,851 --> 00:22:34,686
<i>‪I finished that one easily.</i>

494
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:38,690
‪Has anyone finished one yet?

495
00:22:39,524 --> 00:22:40,817
‪Not even a single one.

496
00:22:40,901 --> 00:22:42,861
‪I haven't finished a single one.

497
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:45,322
‪Let's not ask meaningless questions.

498
00:22:45,906 --> 00:22:47,616
‪I got one done.

499
00:22:47,699 --> 00:22:49,076
‪You did?

500
00:22:49,159 --> 00:22:50,452
‪How?

501
00:22:50,535 --> 00:22:54,414
<i>‪Puzzles like this</i>
<i>‪tend to be closely tied to math,</i>

502
00:22:54,498 --> 00:22:57,834
<i>‪so I figured Hyun-min would do well.</i>

503
00:22:58,418 --> 00:23:00,212
‪How does this even become symmetrical?

504
00:23:00,712 --> 00:23:02,089
‪To make this symmetrical…

505
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:05,884
‪How does this piece fit?

506
00:23:34,538 --> 00:23:37,582
<i>‪I figured out</i>
<i>‪the blue and red ones pretty easily,</i>

507
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:39,835
<i>‪so I thought I might have a chance.</i>

508
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:44,840
‪I don't even know where to begin.

509
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:48,718
‪Damn it. I'm so lost.

510
00:23:50,053 --> 00:23:52,180
‪These sides don't line up at all.
‪What am I supposed to do?

511
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:55,058
‪I need to think it through.

512
00:23:55,142 --> 00:23:56,560
‪If it's symmetrical…

513
00:23:59,437 --> 00:24:01,064
‪Wait, is that it?

514
00:24:01,731 --> 00:24:04,609
<i>‪I think I somehow</i>
<i>‪stumbled on the solution by chance.</i>

515
00:24:05,193 --> 00:24:08,738
<i>‪It felt like it took me about 30 minutes</i>
<i>‪to solve the blue one.</i>

516
00:24:09,322 --> 00:24:10,157
‪Anyone get one?

517
00:24:11,241 --> 00:24:14,161
‪I <i>‪just</i>‪ got one. I think this is right.

518
00:24:15,412 --> 00:24:16,538
‪Have you not completed any?

519
00:24:17,122 --> 00:24:18,957
‪I got one.

520
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,501
<i>‪I didn't see any reason</i>

521
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:23,545
<i>‪to become a target of envy.</i>

522
00:24:24,171 --> 00:24:27,716
<i>‪I knew both of them</i>
<i>‪were good at stuff like this.</i>

523
00:24:27,799 --> 00:24:30,677
<i>‪That's also partly why</i>
<i>‪I didn't tell them about my progress.</i>

524
00:24:32,345 --> 00:24:33,555
‪Why is this so hard?

525
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:38,935
<i>‪Of the three,</i>
<i>‪I think green was the hardest.</i>

526
00:24:39,019 --> 00:24:42,063
<i>‪There were no clean angles</i>
<i>‪you could make out.</i>

527
00:24:43,064 --> 00:24:45,734
‪How are you supposed to
‪line any of this up?

528
00:24:46,443 --> 00:24:49,905
<i>‪The green puzzle didn't consist</i>
<i>‪of regular triangles or rectangles.</i>

529
00:24:49,988 --> 00:24:51,823
<i>‪They had jagged edges.</i>

530
00:24:52,407 --> 00:24:54,367
‪I keep ending up with this.
‪This is so annoying.

531
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:58,288
<i>‪Every layout led me to a crown.</i>

532
00:24:58,371 --> 00:24:59,748
<i>‪It was infuriating.</i>

533
00:24:59,831 --> 00:25:01,833
‪Man, this is just impossible.

534
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:04,211
‪I honestly don't think
‪the green one is solvable.

535
00:25:04,294 --> 00:25:06,087
‪My brain is melting.

536
00:25:06,630 --> 00:25:09,216
‪Damn it. I really wanna figure this out.

537
00:25:11,426 --> 00:25:15,013
<i>‪Relying on instinct alone</i>
<i>‪wasn't cutting it,</i>

538
00:25:15,096 --> 00:25:17,599
<i>‪so I flipped them over</i>
<i>‪to see if they'd line up.</i>

539
00:25:17,682 --> 00:25:20,602
<i>‪I figured wherever the angles lined up</i>
<i>‪when they were overlapped</i>

540
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:22,187
<i>‪should mark the axis of symmetry.</i>

541
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:24,940
<i>‪That's the strategy I went with.</i>

542
00:25:33,490 --> 00:25:34,324
‪No way.

543
00:25:34,991 --> 00:25:36,326
‪I finished one.

544
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:37,869
‪The green one.

545
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:39,955
‪This is insane.

546
00:25:40,038 --> 00:25:40,872
‪Really?

547
00:25:41,498 --> 00:25:42,832
‪You got the green one?

548
00:25:43,875 --> 00:25:45,293
<i>‪Turns out the green one</i>

549
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:46,670
<i>‪was solvable after all.</i>

550
00:25:46,753 --> 00:25:49,547
‪Of course, survival was important,

551
00:25:49,631 --> 00:25:51,800
‪but I was stunned
‪that he actually figured it out.

552
00:25:52,384 --> 00:25:53,593
<i>‪I was so envious.</i>

553
00:26:01,851 --> 00:26:02,936
‪This must be it.

554
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:05,814
<i>‪Kim Dong-jae,</i>

555
00:26:07,565 --> 00:26:08,775
<i>‪you have survived.</i>

556
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:11,987
<i>‪Please remain at your spot.</i>

557
00:26:12,612 --> 00:26:13,780
‪How did you figure it out?

558
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:18,660
<i>‪It's been a while since I placed first.</i>

559
00:26:18,743 --> 00:26:19,995
<i>‪It felt really good.</i>

560
00:26:20,078 --> 00:26:23,999
<i>‪I think it also fired up</i>
<i>‪my competitive spirit.</i>

561
00:26:25,834 --> 00:26:27,085
‪How'd he figure it out?

562
00:26:29,296 --> 00:26:30,463
‪JAE JAE, did you finish red?

563
00:26:30,964 --> 00:26:31,840
‪Yeah.

564
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:34,175
‪I just can't figure out the green.

565
00:26:34,676 --> 00:26:36,052
‪What the heck is this?

566
00:26:37,012 --> 00:26:38,847
‪I feel like I've tried out 300 layouts.

567
00:26:39,431 --> 00:26:42,058
<i>‪I just couldn't figure it out.</i>
<i>‪It really was the ultimate puzzle.</i>

568
00:26:44,227 --> 00:26:45,603
‪Come on.

569
00:26:45,687 --> 00:26:47,897
<i>‪I wanted to figure it out so badly,</i>

570
00:26:47,981 --> 00:26:49,232
<i>‪but nothing was working.</i>

571
00:27:06,374 --> 00:27:07,334
‪Is this it?

572
00:27:08,626 --> 00:27:09,544
<i>‪JAE JAE,</i>

573
00:27:11,046 --> 00:27:12,005
<i>‪you have survived.</i>

574
00:27:12,088 --> 00:27:15,383
‪-No way.
<i>‪-That concludes the exile zone match.</i>

575
00:27:15,467 --> 00:27:18,011
<i>‪Farewell, Oh Hyun-min.</i>

576
00:27:18,094 --> 00:27:19,304
‪Okay.

577
00:27:19,888 --> 00:27:21,431
‪Goodbye, Hyun-min.

578
00:27:22,015 --> 00:27:22,932
‪Thank you.

579
00:27:23,558 --> 00:27:24,601
‪Good luck.

580
00:27:24,684 --> 00:27:29,147
‪JAE JAE, just think of it
‪as filling one row with one to seven,

581
00:27:29,230 --> 00:27:30,607
‪and then pushing it up incrementally.

582
00:27:31,191 --> 00:27:32,108
‪Okay.

583
00:27:32,734 --> 00:27:36,279
<i>‪I noticed JAE JAE's approach</i>
<i>‪to the magic square</i>

584
00:27:36,363 --> 00:27:38,907
<i>‪was just grinding it out,</i>

585
00:27:38,990 --> 00:27:40,658
<i>‪and I felt bad for her.</i>

586
00:27:40,742 --> 00:27:42,619
‪So I tried to explain the method

587
00:27:43,244 --> 00:27:45,163
‪for solving the seven-by-seven version
‪as quickly as I could.

588
00:27:45,246 --> 00:27:47,332
‪But I'm not sure if she understood it.

589
00:27:47,916 --> 00:27:52,253
<i>‪I think JAE JAE is an excellent player,</i>

590
00:27:52,337 --> 00:27:57,258
<i>‪and I hope she can find the composure</i>
<i>‪to make it all the way to the end.</i>

591
00:27:58,218 --> 00:27:59,469
‪I don't have…

592
00:28:01,554 --> 00:28:02,597
‪any regrets

593
00:28:03,181 --> 00:28:05,016
‪about joining <i>‪The Devil's Plan.</i>

594
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:07,519
‪I enjoyed every single moment I was here.

595
00:28:10,397 --> 00:28:14,275
‪Oh man, I get to breathe
‪the air of the living area again.

596
00:28:15,652 --> 00:28:16,903
‪My goodness.

597
00:28:17,987 --> 00:28:19,364
‪This is rough.

598
00:28:20,865 --> 00:28:22,117
‪Good work today.

599
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:23,910
‪Thanks. You too.

600
00:28:24,494 --> 00:28:26,579
‪Poor John has never been up here.

601
00:28:27,455 --> 00:28:30,291
‪Then you should've given it to John.

602
00:28:30,375 --> 00:28:31,626
‪It wouldn't have mattered.

603
00:28:31,709 --> 00:28:33,002
‪-Then I wouldn't have used it.
‪-What?

604
00:28:33,086 --> 00:28:34,045
‪Not if you had chosen John.

605
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:35,380
‪-Come on now.
‪-I'm serious.

606
00:28:38,091 --> 00:28:41,261
‪I genuinely feel bad for XITSUH,

607
00:28:41,344 --> 00:28:44,139
<i>‪but I figured not letting</i>
<i>‪a single one of Dong-min's lackeys</i>

608
00:28:44,222 --> 00:28:46,599
<i>‪stay up in the living area</i>

609
00:28:46,683 --> 00:28:49,102
‪would be a powerful blow on its own.

610
00:28:49,185 --> 00:28:51,354
‪So I decided it was the right time
‪for me to use the token

611
00:28:51,980 --> 00:28:54,190
‪and take a place in the living area.

612
00:28:55,942 --> 00:28:59,487
<i>‪Won-young has once again</i>
<i>‪reduced my efforts to nothing.</i>

613
00:28:59,571 --> 00:29:02,073
‪There's only one thing
‪that has been going my way

614
00:29:02,157 --> 00:29:03,992
‪since I've been here.

615
00:29:04,075 --> 00:29:06,202
‪I said I'd place first, and I have.

616
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:09,289
‪Besides that, nothing has gone right.

617
00:29:11,624 --> 00:29:15,170
‪If I'm this disappointed,

618
00:29:15,253 --> 00:29:18,590
‪just imagine how disappointed
‪XITSUH must be.

619
00:29:18,673 --> 00:29:20,383
‪This can't be!

620
00:29:21,009 --> 00:29:23,344
‪I'd finally been given one!

621
00:29:23,428 --> 00:29:24,637
‪Would you like a tour?

622
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:26,973
‪He snatched it away right in front of me.

623
00:29:27,599 --> 00:29:29,017
‪It was all in vain.

624
00:29:30,602 --> 00:29:32,812
‪Poor XITSUH.

625
00:29:32,896 --> 00:29:34,647
‪That was the funniest thing ever.

626
00:29:34,731 --> 00:29:37,108
‪If I had known,
‪I would've acted all generous and said,

627
00:29:37,192 --> 00:29:38,610
‪"Dong-min, you should give it
‪to Yurisa again."

628
00:29:39,194 --> 00:29:40,487
‪"Let her achieve a hat trick."

629
00:29:40,570 --> 00:29:42,781
‪"I'll gladly play another game today."

630
00:29:42,864 --> 00:29:43,948
‪But instead, I was all…

631
00:29:44,574 --> 00:29:46,659
‪-"Thank you so much."
‪-"Thank you, Dong-min."

632
00:29:46,743 --> 00:29:49,287
‪I bowed so low that my head
‪almost hit the floor, damn it.

633
00:29:49,370 --> 00:29:50,455
‪Out of nowhere,

634
00:29:50,538 --> 00:29:54,626
‪Won-young went, "I think it's time,"
‪and took out this tiny thing.

635
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:56,002
‪-What? So that's it?
‪-What is that?

636
00:29:56,085 --> 00:29:58,588
<i>‪For a second,</i>
<i>‪I thought he took out a piece of candy.</i>

637
00:30:01,007 --> 00:30:04,260
‪Then they announced he used
‪the salvation token or something.

638
00:30:04,344 --> 00:30:06,763
‪I get that he had to use it,
‪but it's still really annoying.

639
00:30:06,846 --> 00:30:07,931
‪Did it have to be today?

640
00:30:08,473 --> 00:30:09,682
‪He could've used it earlier.

641
00:30:10,266 --> 00:30:12,727
‪Hey, newbie, go and get changed.

642
00:30:12,811 --> 00:30:14,896
‪-This place has rules.
‪-Yeah, you need to get changed.

643
00:30:15,563 --> 00:30:18,650
‪If you don't get changed,
‪you'll get the punishment token.

644
00:30:19,692 --> 00:30:20,944
‪What's that?

645
00:30:21,027 --> 00:30:22,654
‪You stand in the corner
‪with your hands up.

646
00:30:23,404 --> 00:30:25,615
‪Keep at it for an hour,
‪or you get eliminated.

647
00:30:26,741 --> 00:30:27,784
‪I'm so bored.

648
00:30:30,453 --> 00:30:31,913
‪What are you guys doing?

649
00:30:32,664 --> 00:30:33,665
‪Where did they go?

650
00:30:33,748 --> 00:30:35,083
‪You must be kidding me.

651
00:30:38,336 --> 00:30:39,212
‪Practice.

652
00:30:45,593 --> 00:30:46,845
‪Practice.

653
00:30:46,928 --> 00:30:47,762
‪Wall…

654
00:30:49,264 --> 00:30:50,265
‪Unbelievable.

655
00:30:52,183 --> 00:30:53,268
‪This.

656
00:30:54,936 --> 00:30:56,646
‪-Wanna play a round?
‪-You wanna?

657
00:30:57,146 --> 00:30:58,606
‪-Let's.
‪-I'm really bad at it though.

658
00:30:59,399 --> 00:31:00,900
‪She can only survive

659
00:31:01,609 --> 00:31:02,777
‪if the game…

660
00:31:02,861 --> 00:31:04,654
‪-Isn't Wall Go II?
‪-Right.

661
00:31:04,737 --> 00:31:06,823
‪-Even so, there are three players.
‪-With three people?

662
00:31:06,906 --> 00:31:09,742
‪-They can team up two-against-one.
‪-XITSUH just needs to back her up.

663
00:31:09,826 --> 00:31:11,244
‪But I'm not sure

664
00:31:12,579 --> 00:31:17,500
‪if he's good enough
‪to pull that off right now.

665
00:31:24,132 --> 00:31:25,508
‪If the game allows it,

666
00:31:25,592 --> 00:31:27,760
‪should we team up?

667
